<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) LOWERS GASOLINE PRICES.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) LOWERS GASOLINE PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) will decrease gasoline prices by 0.30 drachmas per litre, effective on Thursday.</p>
<p>Heating fuel prices will be cut by 2.40 drachmas and transport diesel by 2.3 drachmas per litre, it said.</p>
<p>The price adjustments come after lower world gasoline and diesel prices, down by $0.8 and $8.4 per metric tonne, a lower dollar/drachma exchange rate, down by 0.40 drachmas, DEP said. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
